*$
* OPAx320-Q1 -- LTspice port of TI's PSpice macromodel
*****************************************************************************
* (C) Copyright 2022 Texas Instruments Incorporated. All rights reserved.
* Original: TI PSpice model, Final 1.7, 17JUN2022, datasheet SLOS884B.
* Green-Williams-Lis op amp macro-model architecture.
* TI's disclaimer applies: provided as-is, no warranty of any kind.
*****************************************************************************
* PSpice -> LTspice conversion notes (what changed and why):
*
* 1. R_NOISELESS: PSpice used ".MODEL R_NOISELESS RES(T_ABS=-273.15)" to make
*    the macromodel's internal resistors noise-free so that only the VNSE/FEMT
*    blocks set en/in. LTspice has no RES model, so each resistor instead
*    carries the (undocumented but reliable) "noiseless" attribute:
*      R_R1 IN+ ESDP 10M noiseless
*    Same effect: zero thermal noise contribution in .noise.
*
* 2. G/E ... VALUE={...} -> B-sources (Bxxx n+ n- I=... / V=...).
*    Current direction convention is identical (n+ -> n- through the source),
*    so no sign changes were needed.
*
* 3. PSpice "G1 a b TABLE {expr} = (x,y)(x,y)..." -> LTspice table(x, ...).
*    Both hold the endpoint value outside the table range, so the CLAW curves
*    behave the same at the rails.
*
* 4. LIMIT(x,lo,hi) -> limit(x,lo,hi). LTspice's limit() returns the middle of
*    the three arguments, which equals PSpice's clamp as long as lo < hi
*    (true everywhere here).
*
* 5. VSWITCH models -> LTspice SW models, using
*      Vt = (VON+VOFF)/2 and Vh = -(VON-VOFF)/2
*    The negative Vh gives a smooth, hysteresis-free transition over the same
*    control-voltage window PSpice used, which is what these ESD / overload
*    switches assume.
*
* 6. PWR(x,y) (= |x|^y in PSpice) -> explicit arithmetic: PWR(NVRF,2) is now
*    NVRF*NVRF, and PWR(FLW,0.5)/1E11 in the DVN flicker-noise diode was
*    evaluated at FLW=10 and hardcoded as KF=3.16227766E-11, because LTspice
*    is unreliable about expressions inside .MODEL that reference subcircuit
*    parameters. FLW is still on the VNSE parameter list for compatibility but
*    no longer drives KF -- if you ever change FLW, update KF to sqrt(FLW)/1E11.
*
* 7. Node/port names containing '+' or '-' that appeared *inside* behavioral
*    expressions were renamed (VC+ -> VCP, IOUT- -> IOUTN, etc.) so LTspice's
*    expression parser cannot mistake them for operators. Port ORDER is
*    unchanged, so every instance line still connects identically. The pins of
*    the top-level subcircuit (IN+ IN- VCC VEE OUT) are untouched.
*
* 8. Internal node "SW_OL_OPAx320-Q1" (same string as a subcircuit name) was
*    renamed SW_OL_NODE. The VOS_DRIFT parameter "DC" was renamed VOSDC to
*    avoid colliding with the DC keyword.
*
* 9. "PARAMS:" removed from X instance lines (kept on .SUBCKT lines, where
*    LTspice requires it) and the "DC" keyword dropped from I sources.
*
* Usage: put this file next to your .asc (or in
* ~/Library/Application Support/LTspice/lib/sub on macOS) and add
*   .include OPAx320-Q1.lib
* Pin order: IN+  IN-  VCC  VEE  OUT
*****************************************************************************
.SUBCKT OPAx320-Q1 IN+ IN- VCC VEE OUT
*****************************************************************************
C_C1 N24458 N24659 61.213F
